      "subtitle": "Series 1: 10. 2009",
      "synopses": {
       "large": "Lucy Owen explores BBC Wales’s archives of 2009, with gems that include the BBC Wales presenters in a Strictly dance-off for Children in Need. \n\nThe wild Kashmir goats of Llandudno provide a new regimental mascot for the Royal Welsh. Boffins in Aberystwyth wonder if elephant grass could provide a new biofuel, and we observe Harry Potter’s shell house in Pembrokeshire. \n\nThe Institute of Astronomy donates a giant telescope to Knighton, and the best private collection of Welsh quilts goes on public show. There’s a skunk on the loose in Tredegar, and the women’s tug o’ war team train for the World Championships.",
       "small": "BBC Wales presenters take part in a Strictly dance-off for Children in Need. ",
       "medium": "Lucy Owen takes a personal trip through the BBC Wales news and entertainment archives of 2009, including BBC Wales presenters taking part in a Strictly dance-off for Children in Need. "
